course: dictionary
lesson: 10652
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Unity» means being joined together as one, or people agreeing and working together. A family, a team, a country or a church can all show unity when they stand together.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «Proclaimed unity in Kyiv, but war split them again» tells you that unity is something good that can be broken. When people split apart, they lose their unity. Try swapping in "togetherness": the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, so context tells you which one you need. In a story about people, unity means working together. In a maths sum or an old maths book, unity means the number one. Ask yourself: are the words about people, or about numbers?
fact: Unity means being joined together as one, or people working together.
fact: «Unity» can also mean the number one, especially in old maths books.
fact: «Unity is strength» is a saying: a group that works together is stronger.
fact: 22 January is now celebrated as the Day of Unity, after the day in 1919 when the two Ukrainian republics proclaimed unity.
fact: «Ecumenism» means churches working together and seeking unity, for example in shared services and charities.
exercise: «The two republics proclaimed unity in Kyiv, but war split them again.» What does unity mean here? | Being hungry | Being very loud | *Being joined together as one | Being far away from each other
exercise: In an old maths book, the word «unity» is used for a number. Which number? | Zero | Two | *One | Ten
exercise: Which sentence shows unity? | Each child went home early and did not play | Each child in the team hid the ball from the others | Each child argued about who was the best | *Each child in the team passed the ball so the whole team could win
test: «Unity is strength» means that a group that works together is | Sadder | *Stronger | Quieter | Weaker
test: «Ecumenism means churches working together and seeking unity.» What does ecumenism mean? | Churches with very tall towers | *Churches working together and seeking unity | Churches that only meet on Sundays | Churches closing their doors and keeping apart
exam: Which sentence uses unity to mean the number one? | The team showed a great spirit of unity at the match. | The churches came together in unity for a shared charity service. | The national unity of the country was shown at the big parade. | *In the old maths book, the sum was written as unity plus nothing, so the answer was unity.
